step	21	-	Quick guide step 21
line	<str>Speak to the Dwarven Boatman. (DKS then go through the tunnel to the south west. Once inside proceed through the Cave Entrance directly ahead between the two statues. )</str>
line	
line	<str>Finish the conversation with Commander Veldaban.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Blasidar the sculptor on the east side of Keldagrim, south of the kebab shop.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Vermundi, the silk trader in the eastern market. (Big building east side of river, silk icon)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the Librarian in the library, located at the north-east corner of West Keldagrim.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb any bookcase to find a book on costumes known as the 'Scholars Guide to Dwarven Costumes'.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you didn't bring coal, mine in the north-east corner of East Keldagrim or purchase from Ordan in the Blast Furnace.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Vermundi again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your coal and logs on the spinning machine next to Vermundi then light it with a tinderbox.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Vermundi again and pay 200gp for exquisite clothes.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you didn't bring the 3 Sapphires, they can be purchased from Hervi at the Gem stall just to the north of Vermundi.</str>
line	
line	<str>While here, steal from the baker's or crafting stall for completion of a task in the Easy Fremennik Diary (optional)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Saro at the anvil south-west of the bank in West Keldagrim.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Dromund in the house just north of the bank.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the left boot when he isn't looking.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go outside behind his house and telegrab the right boot through the window when he isn't looking.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Santiri at the weapon shop in north-western West Keldagrim.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use your 3 sapphires on the axe (now in your inventory) and talk to him again.</str>
line	
line	<str>If you have not completed The Knight's Sword Quest then you must speak to the librarian and then to Reldo in Varrock Library.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Thurgo at Mudskipper Point (AIQ), and give him an iron bar to repair the axe. ( May need a redberry pie if Thurgo has not received one recently).</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>You will be given the option to immediately return to Keldagrim; do so.</col>
